ZERO Tor boundary

GOAL
  Define a narrow, auditable boundary between the browser and Tor transport.

RULES
  Browser code does not bypass Tor security controls.
  Tor transport is isolated from rendering and accessibility.
  DNS, proxy and connection failures remain explicit.
  Onion destinations are treated as destinations, not as semantic privileges.
  No automatic identity disclosure.
  No automatic credential submission.

ACCESSIBILITY
  Connection state is exposed as semantic events:
    disconnected
    connecting
    connected
    blocked
    failed
    retrying

VERIFICATION
  Test first against local/non-sensitive endpoints.
  Then test Tor connectivity in a controlled environment.
  Do not claim anonymity merely because a connection succeeded.
